remstart
    THE SHOP
    the upgrade screen is the angler's shop. it is there at every upgrade screen, and it never holds
    anything up, and it does not say anything unless it is asked. the routines are in fish_routines_shop.

    it is the guide (see fish_headers_guide), with GUIDE_SHOP on, so the words wait in the same line. the
    upgrade screen has a loop of its own, so frame_guide does not run: frame_ability_selection comes to
    frame_shop instead. everything is drawn to TARGET_UPGRADE, so that the wave of bubbles brings it in.
    guideOff puts it all back.

    THE FIRST ONE. the first upgrade screen of a game that had the tutorial has the angler in the corner,
    next to the title, with the words under it that say how to ask it. there is a scene of its own first,
    before the cards: see THE FIRST UPGRADE in fish_routines_intro. here it only says that it can be asked.

    THE DEEP. every other one is deeper (SHOP_ROAM): the water is much darker, the corners of the dark
    backdrop close in (DeepEffect.fx, which is under the cards and the words, unlike a screen effect), and
    the angler swims around in the dark behind the cards, with only its light for company. how to ask it
    is in the hints along the bottom. when it has something to say, it swims up to the corner to say it.

    THE QUESTION. the info key, or a click on the angler, brings it for real: the dark comes down over the
    upgrade screen, and it swims in with its scene, the same one that the card brings (angler_run, with
    ANGLER_FROM_SHOP). the questions are up to three, and a line that goes back. they are only about
    things that the player has seen, and has not asked about yet. shopPickTopics finds them: first what
    happened lately, from ANGLER_RECENT, newest first, then what is on the board, then anything else that
    the player can see. it is never a rumor. rumors are what the card, and a kept light, are for. it
    answers one on every upgrade screen, and it all goes on rnd, never on a stream. going back without
    asking does not use it up.

    the things that happened are noted with anglerNote. they last for one game, and they are not saved.
    a game that is carried on later starts with none, and goes by the board.
remend

global SHOP_ENABLED = 1 `0 and the angler is not at the upgrade screen. the tests turn it off.
global GUIDE_SHOP = 0 `1 while the guide is at the upgrade screen
global SHOP_ROAM = 0 `1 while it swims around in the dark. see THE DEEP.
global SHOP_ASKED = 0 `1 once the question of this upgrade screen has been asked
global SHOP_HIDDEN = 0 `1 while a page of its own is up over the upgrade screen, like the book
global SHOP_BOX_OPEN = 0 `1 while its box is up, or on its way up
global SHOP_CLOSE_MS = 0 `when the box goes, once the words are out, or 0 until then
global SHOP_TITLE_KEEP# = 1 `how much of the title shows, while the box goes over it
global SHOP_ASK_TEXT_ID = 0 `the words under the angler that say how to ask it, on the first upgrade screen

` where it sits to talk. the cards take up the middle, and there can be four of them, so the top is what is left.
global SHOP_X = 6
global SHOP_Y = 8
global SHOP_BOX_X = 150
global SHOP_BOX_Y = 2
global SHOP_BOX_H = 96 `room for the four lines of an answer, or for a line and the questions

` where it swims
global SHOP_SWIM_X# = 0
global SHOP_SWIM_Y# = 0
global SHOP_GO_X# = 0 `where it is headed
global SHOP_GO_Y# = 0
global SHOP_FACE_LEFT = 0 `1 while it looks left
global SHOP_LAST_MS = 0 `the last frame that it moved on
global SHOP_ROAM_SPEED# = 22 `how fast it swims around, in pixels every second
global SHOP_RUSH_SPEED# = 170 `and how fast it comes when it is asked

` how deep it is, from 0 to 1. it comes on over SHOP_DEEP_MS once the wave has gone.
global SHOP_DEEP# = 0
global SHOP_DEEP_MS = 900
global SHOP_DEEP_FX_ID = 0 `what closes the corners in, on the dark backdrop of the upgrade screen
global SHOP_DIM_ALPHA = 200 `how dark the middle of the deep is

` what has happened lately, newest first. -1 is nothing. the numbers are topics of the angler.
global SHOP_RECENT_ROOM = 8
global dim ANGLER_RECENT(8)
